                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>25.37658,57.147971,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark></Folder><Folder><name><![CDATA[Ancient Village or Settlement]]></name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>   <name>Pokaini Forest</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>Alt Name:</b> Pokainu Mezs <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>5</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 56.571039 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 23.075712<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Eastern_Europe/Latvia/thumb/yzv_1_2.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Inside the Pokaini forest there are Standing stones, stones forming groups, piles, walls and rivers: the Pokaini Stone Agglomerates. These were the main reason why the Pokaini Forest is connected with...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=46180" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>23.075712,56.571039,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark></Folder><Folder><name><![CDATA[Barrow Cemetery]]></name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>   <name>Grobina</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Barrow Cemetery <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 56.53144 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 21.18973<br />
                    Barrow Cemetery in Latvia. Group of barrow cemeteries near Grobina belongs to the most important archaeological sites in Latvia. The barrows are dated for 5th - 13th century AC, but during the excavat...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
