<Placemark>   <name>Meldzeres dobumakmens</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Holed Stone <b>Alt Name:</b> Hollow Stone of Meldzeres <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 56.4982 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 21.9581<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Eastern_Europe/Latvia/thumb/DSCF7998.r9.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Cup stones are not rare on the Eastern shores of the Baltic Sea.  They all have approximately the same dimensions.  They are considered precious enough testimonies of the past for some of them to be n...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
